 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>A <b>Layout Manager</b> decides the size and position of components inside a container. It is set with <code>setLayout()</code>.</p><h3>Points</h3><ul><li>Components resize/move automatically when the window size changes.</li><li><code>setLayout(null)</code> = absolute positioning with setBounds().</li></ul><table><tr><th>Layout</th><th>How it arranges</th></tr><tr><td><b>FlowLayout</b></td><td>Left to right in a row, wraps (default for JPanel)</td></tr><tr><td><b>BorderLayout</b></td><td>North, South, East, West, Center (default for JFrame)</td></tr><tr><td><b>GridLayout</b></td><td>Rows × columns of equal cells</td></tr><tr><td><b>CardLayout</b></td><td>Stack of cards, one visible at a time</td></tr><tr><td><b>GridBagLayout</b></td><td>Flexible grid, cells can span rows/cols</td></tr><tr><td><b>BoxLayout</b></td><td>Single row or column</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
